<h4 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Patient Procedures</h4>

<div class="etl-guide-columns">
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <!-- Important Notes -->
    <div class="bg-yellow-500/20 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-400/30">
      <h5 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 text-yellow-300">Important Notes</h5>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li>• Contains standardized procedural billing codes (HCPCS) for hospitalizations</li>
        <li>• Only includes procedures that were <strong>performed/completed</strong> (not cancelled)</li>
        <li>• <strong>Includes:</strong> <strong>all</strong> CPT codes (HCPCS Level 1), both those billed by clinicians (professional billing) and those recorded in hospital billing encounters (e.g., PT/OT codes). Do not filter to a subset of codes.</li>
        <li>• <strong>Excludes:</strong> HCPCS Level 2 products, supplies and services that have no CPT code</li>
        <li>• Also contains <strong>ICD-10-PCS</strong> procedure codes (used for DRG calculation, may appear in hospital_diagnosis)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 1 -->
    <div>
      <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 1: Pull Every Procedure Code</h5>
      <p class="text-sm mb-3">Pull every completed procedure code from <strong>both</strong> professional billing and hospital billing sources. Unlike earlier versions, 3.0 does not restrict the table to a code list: ETL every CPT code and every ICD-10-PCS code.</p>
      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-sm">
        <p class="text-xs mb-1">The mCIDE folder still carries a short reference list of procedure codes. In 3.0 it is <strong>not</strong> an inclusion filter.</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/Common-Longitudinal-ICU-data-Format/CLIF/blob/3.0/mCIDE/patient_procedures/clif_patient_procedure_codes.csv" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline text-xs">→ clif_patient_procedure_codes.csv</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 2 -->
    <div>
      <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 2: Filter to Inpatient Hospitalizations</h5>
      <p class="text-sm">Filter to inpatient hospitalizations. Keep all codes for those hospitalizations.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 3 -->
    <div>
      <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 3: Remove Cancelled Procedures</h5>
      <div class="bg-yellow-500/20 p-3 rounded-lg border border-yellow-400/30 text-sm">
        <p><strong>Do not include cancelled CPT codes.</strong> A procedure that was cancelled was not performed, so its code does not belong in this table. Use the status in your source billing data to find cancelled codes and leave those rows out.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-6">
    <!-- Step 4 -->
    <div>
      <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 4: Populate the 3.0 Columns</h5>
      <p class="text-sm mb-3">The 3.0 table has six columns:</p>
      <div class="bg-white/10 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs space-y-1">
        <div>• <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">hospitalization_id</span></div>
        <div>• <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">billing_provider_id</span> — ID of the provider who billed the procedure</div>
        <div>• <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">performing_provider_id</span> — ID of the provider who performed it</div>
        <div>• <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">procedure_code</span> — the code itself (valid CPT, ICD-10-PCS or HCPCS code)</div>
        <div>• <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">procedure_code_format</span> — one of <span class="font-mono">CPT</span>, <span class="font-mono">ICD10PCS</span>, <span class="font-mono">HCPCS</span></div>
        <div>• <span class="font-mono text-yellow-300">procedure_billed_dttm</span> — when the procedure was billed (may differ from when it was performed), in UTC</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step 5 -->
    <div>
      <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Step 5: Final Cleanup</h5>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
          <strong>Deduplicate:</strong> Remove duplicate rows
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
          <strong>UTC Conversion:</strong> Convert all datetime fields to UTC timezone
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">•</span>
          <strong>Data Types:</strong> Ensure all variables match data dictionary specifications
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Date-Only Columns Tip -->
    <div class="bg-blue-500/20 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-400/30">
      <h5 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 text-blue-300">Date-Only Columns</h5>
      <p class="text-sm mb-2">When your source data only contains a date (no time component):</p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li>• Set the time to midnight (00:00:00) in your local timezone</li>
        <li>• Make it timezone-aware</li>
        <li>• Then convert to UTC</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-sm mt-3 text-blue-200">
        <strong>Example:</strong> A date of 2021-08-26 becomes 2021-08-26 00:00:00 local time,
        which converts to 2021-08-26 05:00:00+00:00 UTC (for US/Central timezone).
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Data Quality Checks -->
    <div>
      <h5 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Data Quality Checks</h5>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
          Verify procedure codes are valid CPT, ICD-10-PCS or HCPCS codes and that procedure_code_format matches each code
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
          Ensure only completed procedures are included, with no cancelled CPT codes
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start">
          <span class="text-green-300 mr-2">✓</span>
          Confirm hospital billing CPT codes (e.g., PT/OT) are present, not only professional billing codes
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
